Vendored snapshot of repo.secureblue.dev/repodata/ at the current pin.

  repomd.xml       signed repo index (matches pins.nix versionRelease)
  repomd.xml.asc   secureblue's detached GPG signature over repomd.xml
  primary.xml.zst  the package list repomd.xml's <checksum> vouches for
                   (upstream name a8fd0abb...-primary.xml.zst; identity here
                    is the path, integrity is the checksum inside repomd.xml)

lib/verify.nix layer 2 GPG-verifies these against the pinned secureblue key and
binds the pinned RPM's sha256 to the <checksum> primary.xml lists for this arch.
They are vendored (not fetched) because repo.secureblue.dev rewrites repomd.xml
on every publish of any version -- a live fetch breaks the build on every
upstream release.

Refreshed automatically by `nix run .#update` (verify/10-verify-supply-chain.sh
writes the freshly signature-checked files here). To refresh by hand, run
./verify/10-verify-supply-chain.sh <version-release> <arch> from a checkout.
